<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended down on Thursday after a volatile session with traders eyeing a possible rate cut from the Bank of Spain on Friday.</p>
<p>Dealers said weakness in other markets had weighed on bonos, dragging them lower into the close.</p>
<p>Nervousness ahead of Spain's CPI data and a possible rate cut from the Bank of Spain on Friday had added to the session's volatile mood, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is focusing on tomorrow's events which will excite the market whatever the outcome,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
</text>
